- The Initial Royalty Term for a Product-by-Product and country-by-country basis within the Ono Territory ends on the last of:
  (a) [ * ] thereafter;  
  (b) the expiration of all Valid Claims within the Array Patents that would, but for the license granted under this Agreement, be infringed by the sale or use of such Product in such country;
  (c) the expiration of the Applicable Regulatory Exclusivity Period for such Product in such country.

: If a party is acquired or undergoes a change of control, the contract does not specify what happens under this scenario. However, if either Party (the "Bankrupt Party"), commences or becomes the subject of any case or proceeding under the bankruptcy laws, then upon such breach, the non-defaulting party may terminate the Agreement as follows:

- For a default under clause (i) above, if payment is not made within ten days after the defaulting party shall have received written notice of such failure to make payment;  
- Or for a default under clause (ii) above, if such default is not cured within thirty days after the defaulting party shall have received written notice specifying in reasonable detail the nature of such default and such action the defaulting party must take in order to cure each such item of default.
